    "messages": [
      {
        "content": "Diana gets 30 minutes of video game time for every hour she reads. Her dad decided to raise her reward by 20%. Diana read for 12 hours this week. How many more minutes of video game time will she get as a result of her raise?",
        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": " FINAL: 36",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Given that Diana gets 30 minutes of video game time for every hour she reads, and her dad decided to raise her reward by 20%, we need to find out how many more minutes of video game time she will get as a result of this raise, given that Diana read for 12 hours this week.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the original reward:\n- Original reward per hour of reading: 30 minutes\n- Hours read: 12\n- Original total video game time: \\(30 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 360 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nNext, we calculate the new reward after the 20% increase:\n- Increase in reward: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 0.20 = 6 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n- New reward per hour: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} + 6 \\text{ minutes} = 36 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nNow, we calculate the new total video game time with the increased reward:\n- New total video game time: \\(36 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 432 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nTo find out how many more minutes of video game time she will get as a result of the raise, we subtract the original total from the new total:\n- Additional video game time: \\(432 \\text{ minutes} - 360 \\text{ minutes} = 72 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nThus, Diana will get 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Write your own reusable record: explain the specific operations, when they apply, and a concrete check using this problem. Retain its final answer. Solve in your own first-person voice, using 150–400 tokens. Identify the given quantities and requested unknown, explain the actual reusable operations connecting them, and check the result against the problem. Do not pad with generic advice or invent observations. Finish with a separate line FINAL: followed by just the numeric answer.",
        "role": "user"
      }
    ],
    "prompt_tokens": 557,
    "raw": "Given quantities:\n- Original reward: 30 minutes of video game time for every hour read\n- Increase in reward: 20%\n- Hours read: 12 hours\n\nUnknown:\n- Additional video game time due to the raise\n\nOperations:\n1. Calculate the original total video game time.\n2. Calculate the new reward per hour after the 20% increase.\n3. Calculate the new total video game time.\n4. Subtract the original total from the new total to find the additional video game time.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. Original total video game time: \\(30 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 360 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n2. New reward per hour: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} + (30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 0.20) = 30 \\text{ minutes} + 6 \\text{ minutes} = 36 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n3. New total video game time: \\(36 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 432 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n4. Additional video game time: \\(432 \\text{ minutes} - 360 \\text{ minutes} = 72 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nCheck:\n- Original total: 360 minutes\n- New total: 432 minutes\n- Difference: 432 - 360 = 72 minutes\n\nThus, Diana will get 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
