  "target": "Given quantities:\n- Original reward: 30 minutes of video game time for every hour read\n- Increase in reward: 20%\n- Hours read: 12 hours\n\nUnknown:\n- Additional video game time due to the raise\n\nOperations:\n1. Calculate the original total video game time.\n2. Calculate the new reward per hour after the 20% increase.\n3. Calculate the new total video game time.\n4. Subtract the original total from the new total to find the additional video game time.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. Original total video game time: \\(30 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 360 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n2. New reward per hour: \\(30 \\text{ minutes} + (30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 0.20) = 30 \\text{ minutes} + 6 \\text{ minutes} = 36 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n3. New total video game time: \\(36 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\times 12 \\text{ hours} = 432 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n4. Additional video game time: \\(432 \\text{ minutes} - 360 \\text{ minutes} = 72 \\text{ minutes}\\)\n\nCheck:\n- Original total: 360 minutes\n- New total: 432 minutes\n- Difference: 432 - 360 = 72 minutes\n\nThus, Diana will get 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
